#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# histogram

#% text
# `histogram(data)` draws a bar for each bin of equal width, as high as the number of values in it.

#% text
# `histogram([data1, data2, ...])` draws the histograms of several data sets over each other, half transparent.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is `image("path")`, a PNG file with SVG and PDF copies next to it.

#% item
# Bins include their left end and exclude their right end; their edges are multiples of the width.

#% item
# The automatic width is twice the spread of the middle half of the data over the cube root of the count, rounded up to 1, 2, 2.5 or 5 times a power of ten.

#% item
# Options:

#% subitem
# `bins: n` asks for about n bins of a round width; `bins: [w]` for width w; `bins: [lo, hi, w]` for bins of width w from lo to hi (values outside are left out).

#% subitem
# `normalized: true` scales the bars so that their total area is 1, for comparing with a probability density.

#% subitem
# `colors`, `legend` and the labels work as for `plot`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Two thousand samples of the standard normal distribution:

#% cell
random_seed(3); histogram(random_variate(normal_distribution(0, 1), 2000))
#% output
#= image("histogram.files/histogram-1.png")

#% subsection
# Options

#% text
# Bins of width 1 from 0 to 6 for the throws of a die:

#% cell
random_seed(5); histogram(random_integer([1, 6], 600), bins: [0.5, 6.5, 1])
#% output
#= image("histogram.files/histogram-2.png")

#% text
# Two data sets with a legend:

#% cell
random_seed(8); histogram([random_variate(normal_distribution(0, 1), 800), random_variate(normal_distribution(2, 0.7), 800)], bins: 25, legend: ["first", "second"])
#% output
#= image("histogram.files/histogram-3.png")

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Normalized, the bars approach the density of the distribution:

#% cell
random_seed(4); histogram(random_variate(exponential_distribution(1), 5000), bins: [0.25], normalized: true)
#% output
#= image("histogram.files/histogram-4.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bar_chart`, `list_plot`, `random_variate`
